[0.259, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[4B\r\u001b[5A  Both refactorings tackle the core problem: a God Object exposes too much internal state, encouraging external code to reach in and drive logic from outside. By encapsulating fields behind accessors, you create natural seams to later   \r\u001b[1B  extract\u001b[1Cresponsibilities\u001b[1Cinto\u001b[1Cseparate\u001b[1Cclasses.\r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mPractical next step:\u001b[22m Once fields are encapsulated, apply \u001b[1mExtract Class\u001b[22m (RF-004) to split\u001b[1Ccohesive\u001b[1Cgroups\u001b[1Cof\u001b[1Cfields\u001b[1Cand\u001b[1Cmethods\u001b[1Cinto\u001b[1Cfocused\u001b[1Cobjects\u001b[1C—\u001b[1Cdirectly\u001b[1Cresolving\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1CSRP\u001b[1Cviolation.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B                                             \r\r\n\u001b[2C---\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[1mViolated\u001b[1Claw\u001b[22m\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[2C┌─────┬─────┬─────────────┐\r\r\n\u001b[2C│\u001b"]
